    links=''.join(f'<li><a href="{repo}/blob/main/{path}">{label}</a></li>' for label,path in records)
    page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{esc(d['title'])} | Emmanuel Sampson</title><meta name="description" content="Chicago grocery access, 2021–2025. Verified business events, modeled before-and-after access, neighborhood differences and conditional emissions."><link rel="stylesheet" href="site/style.css"><script src="site/app.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to research</a><header class="nav"><a class="brand" href="#">EMMANUEL SAMPSON / URBAN RESEARCH</a><nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#period">Study period</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="#results">Access</a><a href="#equity">Equity</a><a href="#travel">Emissions</a><a href="#records">Downloads</a></nav></header><main id="main" class="wrap"><section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Chicago · Historical investigation 2021–2025</div><h1>{esc(d['title'])}</h1><p class="lede">{esc(d['subtitle'])}.</p><p class="byline">{esc(d['author'])}<br>University of Pennsylvania<br>{esc(d['publication_status'])} · {esc(d['publication_date'])} · {version}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="outputs/public/Chicago_Grocery_Access_Report.docx">Download the Word report ↓</a><a class="button alt" href="#results">Read the results ↓</a></div></div><aside class="hero-side" aria-label="Main findings"><div><strong>6 events</strong><p>Five closures and one replacement opening at five premises</p></div><div><strong>11.48 → 16.10 min</strong><p>Modeled one-way walking access around the Kenwood Walmart · 22 tract origins</p></div><div><strong>−2.10 min</strong><p>Modeled improvement with the Englewood replacement opening · 14 tract origins</p></div><p class="scope-note">Fixed population weights. Calculated access; actual travel responses remain unmeasured.</p></aside></section><div class="story-guide" aria-label="Follow the findings"><a href="#evidence"><strong>1. Follow the events</strong>Examine the closures, replacement opening and date audit.</a><a href="#results"><strong>2. Compare access</strong>Explore the same tract origins before and after each event.</a><a href="#travel"><strong>3. Assess the implications</strong>Read the neighborhood comparisons and emissions scenarios.</a></div>{''.join(sections)}<section id="references" class="section"><div class="report-section references"><h2>References</h2><p class="mini">Numbers in the text refer to these sources. Actual data acquisition timestamps are retained in the source manifest.</p><ol>{refs}</ol></div></section><section id="records" class="section"><div class="report-section"><h2>Research records and downloads</h2><p>The academic Word and PDF reports share the same narrative and ten figures as this website. Six additional Matplotlib map pairs support the event explorer. Start with notebook 02 for the executed access comparisons. Notebook 03 records the inputs still needed for observed mobility and causal estimates.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="outputs/public/Chicago_Grocery_Access_Report.docx">Word report ↓</a><a class="button alt" href="outputs/public/Chicago_Grocery_Access_Report.pdf">PDF report ↗</a><a class="button alt" href="{repo}">GitHub repository ↗</a></div><ul>{links}<li><a href="{repo}/releases/tag/{version}">Reproducible project package and historical street graphs</a></li></ul><p class="mini">The release includes public processed inputs, executed notebooks, source code and derived historical street graphs. Raw national files can be retrieved with the documented downloader. Licensed mobility source files are excluded. Routes use © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0, via Geofabrik. Original code is MIT licensed; third-party data retain their own terms.</p><details class="mini"><summary>City of Chicago data notice</summary><p>This site provides applications using data that has been modified for use from its original source, www.cityofchicago.org, the official website of the City of Chicago. The City of Chicago makes no claims as to the content, accuracy, timeliness, or completeness of any of the data provided at this site. The data provided at this site is subject to change at any time. It is understood that the data provided at this site is being used at one's own risk.</p></details></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="footer-inner"><strong>{esc(d['author'])} · University of Pennsylvania</strong><p><a href="{repo}">Research code and reproducibility record</a> · {version} · {esc(d['publication_date'])}</p></div></footer></body></html>'''
    (ROOT/'index.html').write_text(page);(ROOT/'.nojekyll').touch()
